[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded voltage-controlled behavioral resistance

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Acceptance target is unchanged original regression/misc/asrc-tc-2.cir, complete
OP and AC observables and original 1e-9 assertions against stock ngspice.
No closure is claimed until the full original executes. Requested frontend stays
OP/DC/AC only; transient and pole-zero refuse. Native device first,
then generated-metadata frontend expression/temperature lowering. Reuse the
existing bounded single-input expression evaluator and four-terminal stamping;
no multivariate language or legacy runtime dependency is introduced. Existing
SpiceSharp/ngspice reuse assessment and retained Rust decision remain applicable.
Pinned RSpice engine/builder/behavioral.rs constructs I=Vout/(Rexpression*scale).
The independent reference is stock ngspice, not copied RSpice runtime behavior.

Affected path: typed Rust/.NET element -> immutable compiled four-terminal model
-> Newton residual and analytic Jacobian -> converged-bias sparse AC matrix ->
physical audit/power -> requested circuit lowering -> native comparator/reporting.
Control is high impedance; output current flows P to N. All voltages are volts,
resistance ohms, current amperes, derivatives siemens. The same derivative must
serve DC and AC, including when control terminals alias output terminals. No
sample-hold, outer iteration, frozen control or discarded AC coupling is allowed.
Pure memoryless resistance adds no charge/history. Native transient capability
must be verified separately; frontend admission stays bounded by actual evidence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIORAL-RESISTANCE-LAW-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Owned memoryless resistance expression
STATEMENT: >>>
A bounded behavioral resistor shall impose I=(Vp-Vn)/R(Vcp-Vcn) with a finite
bounded single-input expression, high-impedance control, and exact output and
control partials. It shall refuse zero resistance, nonfinite values, expression
domain failures and overflow without clamping, substituting zero or publishing
a successful partial result. Finite negative resistance remains an explicit
active law. Structural validation shall not invent a control bias.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: behavioral_resistor, typed circuit variant, compiled
four-terminal stamps. Verification: behavioral_resistor integration tests,
independent analytical derivatives, finite differences and seeded properties.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIORAL-RESISTANCE-AC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Converged-bias incremental resistance law
STATEMENT: >>>
DC residuals and sparse AC conductance shall use the same
signed analytic partials. AC shall evaluate at the converged DC operating point,
including nonzero control excitation and terminal aliasing. Independent DC audits
shall evaluate the physical current and power from terminal voltages and the
resistance expression. Result failure shall remain explicit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: independent dense/Faer DC and AC analytical fixtures, full MNA finite
differences, audit/power checks and unchanged asrc-tc-2 OP/AC. See
evidence/behavioral-resistance.json and docs/behavioral-resistance-results.md.
No campaign deck count or original-program agreement is implied by native tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIORAL-RESISTANCE-TEMP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve resistance temperature scaling in the runtime law
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested explicit R={expression} metadata shall retain every assignment and
physical source range. Qualified TC1/TC2 values shall multiply the full resistance
expression by 1+TC1*dT+TC2*dT^2 with dT=T-27 Celsius before dispatch. Both output
and control partials shall therefore scale inversely through the same native
law. Unknown/duplicate attributes, other runtime variables, multiple independent
control pairs, zero/nonfinite factors and unqualified analyses shall refuse
atomically. Strict non-requested preparation shall retain its existing policy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: generated PrimitiveSyntax/ResistorModelExtraction,
BehavioralResistanceLowering, OperatingPointBridge, RequestedTemperaturePreparation
and RequestedAnalysis. Tests: BehavioralResistanceTests, unchanged asrc-tc-2.cir,
examples/behavioral-resistance.cir. Evidence: behavioral-resistance.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIORAL-RESISTANCE-WIRE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed bounded resistance wire contract
STATEMENT: >>>
The Rust/.NET element contract and checked request schema shall describe one
behavioral_resistor identity, output/control nodes and bounded expression tree.
Unknown fields/operations and malformed node/expression data shall reject.
AC source phasors required for independent control gain shall be represented in
the schema; absence of a phasor retains existing API defaults. Schema acceptance
alone shall not imply domain validity, bounded tree resources or convergence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
